      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wilton began in 1908 when the Central California Traction Railroad built a station on Seth Wilton’s ranch, sparking the town’s first settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://elkgrovehistoricalsociety.com/history-town-of-wilton/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community grew around that station, and today it still hosts the historic Wilton Store and the original post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://elkgrovehistoricalsociety.com/history-town-of-wilton/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every second Saturday of October, the Wilton History Group marks Wilton History Day at the Dillard School, celebrating the town’s heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://elkgrovehistoricalsociety.com/history-town-of-wilton/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wilton lies partly in the Cosumnes River floodplain, and in 2022 residents were evacuated when levees broke during a flood warning.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilton%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Wilton Rancheria, a federally recognized tribe, opened Sky River Casino in 2022 after decades of land trust negotiations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
